---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { balbotDesign } from "../../data/siteContent";

const sections = [
  {
    id: "mechanical-design",
    title: "Mechanical design and component layout",
    paragraphs: [
      "BALBOT brings an ESP32, an MPU6050 IMU, and encoder-equipped geared motors into a two-wheeled platform. The chassis has to support the electronics and power system while leaving room for wiring, access, and mechanical adjustment.",
      "Component placement is part of the control problem. Mass distribution changes how the robot tips and responds; structural flex and loose wiring can introduce movement that the sensor reads as part of the robot’s motion. The aim is a rigid, accessible assembly that can be revised as the hardware is tested.",
    ],
  },
  {
    id: "attitude-estimation",
    title: "IMU calibration and attitude estimation",
    paragraphs: [
      "Tilt is estimated by combining accelerometer and gyroscope measurements in a complementary filter. The gyroscope follows rapid changes in angle, while the accelerometer supplies a longer-term reference that helps limit drift.",
      "Gyroscope bias is measured while the sensor is stationary. Sensor orientation and sign conventions then need to agree with the rest of the control loop. Filter tuning is a balance between responsiveness and noise: an estimate that looks smooth is only useful if it still responds quickly enough to a real disturbance.",
    ],
  },
  {
    id: "motor-control",
    title: "Motor control and encoder feedback",
    paragraphs: [
      "The motor interface turns a signed command into wheel direction and PWM duty cycle. Encoder counts provide a separate measurement of wheel motion, allowing the firmware to estimate speed rather than assume that a PWM command produces a particular response.",
      "Low-speed behavior is especially important. A motor may not move until its command clears a dead zone, and the two motors may respond differently to the same input. Direction checks, stop behavior, encoder signs, and speed estimates need to be established before closing the velocity loop.",
    ],
  },
  {
    id: "controller-tuning",
    title: "Controller design and tuning",
    paragraphs: [
      "The balance controller uses the difference between target and estimated tilt to calculate a corrective command. The intended cascaded structure uses this outer loop to request wheel motion, with an inner velocity loop regulating motor response through encoder feedback.",
      "The PID implementation includes output limits and anti-windup so the integral term does not keep accumulating when the requested correction exceeds the available output. Initial proportional-only checks confirm the direction and scale of the response; physical tuning must then evaluate oscillation, saturation, and recovery together.",
    ],
  },
  {
    id: "telemetry",
    title: "Telemetry and debugging workflow",
    paragraphs: [
      "Serial telemetry exposes estimated tilt, target angle, error, controller output, wheel-speed targets, measured RPM, and PWM commands. Reading these signals together helps distinguish a sensing problem from a motor-response or timing problem.",
      "The workflow is incremental: check the sensor, test actuation, verify encoder feedback, and then integrate the control loops. Keeping those checks separate makes an unexpected response easier to trace than changing the estimator, gains, and motor settings at the same time.",
    ],
  },
  {
    id: "evaluation",
    title: "Test results, limitations, and next revisions",
    paragraphs: [
      "The repository records manual-tilt checks of the proportional controller: opposite tilt directions produce opposite commands, output grows with error, and saturation limits are exercised. These checks validate parts of the implementation; they are not a demonstration of sustained balancing.",
      "Balance duration, tilt error, and disturbance recovery are the next evaluation measures. The next upgrades are telemetry graphs and a portable interface for monitoring signals and reviewing controller behavior during testing.",
    ],
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="BALBOT | Om Anand"
  description="The design and development of BALBOT: a two-wheeled robot exploring mechanical layout, attitude estimation, motor feedback, and embedded control."
  bodyClass="project-case-study balbot-page"
>
  <section class="balbot-hero page-frame" aria-labelledby="balbot-title">
    <a class="balbot-back" href="/#work">
      ← Selected work
    </a>
    <div class="balbot-hero__grid">
      <div class="balbot-hero__copy">
        <div class="balbot-meta">
          <p class="court-label">A study in balance</p>
        </div>
        <h1 id="balbot-title">BALBOT</h1>
        <p class="balbot-intro">
          A small robot, an unstable system, and the work of bringing sensing,
          mechanics, and control into one loop.
        </p>
        <p class="balbot-hardware">
          ESP32 · MPU6050 · Encoder-equipped geared motors
        </p>
      </div>
      <figure class="balbot-design">
        <img
          src={balbotDesign.src}
          alt={balbotDesign.alt}
          width="546"
          height="390"
          fetchpriority="high"
        />
        <figcaption>{balbotDesign.caption}</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <nav
    class="balbot-contents page-frame"
    aria-label="Inside the BALBOT project"
  >
    <p class="court-label">Inside the build</p>
    <ul>
      {sections.map((section) => (
        <li>
          <a href={`#${section.id}`}>{section.title}</a>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </nav>

  <div class="balbot-chapters page-frame">
    {sections.map((section) => (
      <section
        class="balbot-chapter"
        id={section.id}
        aria-labelledby={`${section.id}-heading`}
      >
        <header>
          <h2 id={`${section.id}-heading`}>{section.title}</h2>
        </header>
        <div class="balbot-chapter__body">
          {section.paragraphs.map((paragraph) => (
            <p>{paragraph}</p>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>
    ))}
  </div>

  <section class="balbot-links page-frame" aria-label="Continue exploring">
    <p>Code, implementation notes, and tuning records.</p>
    <a
      class="court-link"
      href="https://github.com/Andromeda-crypto/BALBOT"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
    >
      View the repository ↗
    </a>
    <a class="court-link" href="/#work">
      Back to selected work ↗
    </a>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .balbot-hero {
    padding-top: 8.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 3rem;
  }
  .balbot-hero__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 0.9fr 1.1fr;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    align-items: center;
  }
  .balbot-hero__copy {
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .balbot-design {
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .balbot-design img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
  .balbot-design figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.8rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .balbot-hero__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2rem;
    }
    .balbot-design {
      max-width: 42rem;
    }
  }
  .balbot-back {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }
  .balbot-back:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  .balbot-meta {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  .balbot-hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 6rem);
    margin: 1.2rem 0 1.5rem;
  }
  .balbot-intro {
    max-width: 40rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 2.3vw, 1.9rem);
  }
  .balbot-hardware {
    margin-top: 1.6rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
  .balbot-contents {
    border-top: var(--border-thin);
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }
  .balbot-contents ul {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    column-gap: 3rem;
    row-gap: 0.4rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
  .balbot-contents a {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: baseline;
    padding: 0.4rem 0;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }
  .balbot-contents a:hover {
    color: var(--color-terracotta);
  }
  .balbot-chapter {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 0.85fr 1.15fr;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 5rem);
    border-top: var(--border-thin);
    padding-block: 3rem;
  }
  .balbot-chapter h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
    max-width: 21ch;
  }
  .balbot-chapter__body {
    max-width: 62ch;
  }
  .balbot-chapter__body p + p {
    margin-top: 1.2rem;
  }
  .balbot-links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem 2rem;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    border-top: var(--border-thin);
    padding-block: 2rem 3.5rem;
  }
  .balbot-links > p {
    flex-basis: 100%;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .balbot-hero {
      padding-top: 7rem;
      padding-bottom: 2.5rem;
    }
    .balbot-back {
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }
    .balbot-chapter {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1.5rem;
      padding-block: 2.5rem;
    }
    .balbot-chapter h2 {
      max-width: 24ch;
    }
    .balbot-chapter__body {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }
    .balbot-contents ul {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
